# Internal records · `guide:acts:records`

**Section (Acts)** · `sec:acts:area-acts` {{ row('org.peer-network.testing.claim-areas', owner='RECORDS', area='acts').stake }} The first slice implements local validation under (`[ROOT-sig:design:records]`) and (`[ROOT-model:design:accepted-act]`); it does not certify authentication, formation, membership, family endpoint typing or a standing result.

**Definition (Structural identity)** · `def:acts:identity` An ActId consists of its exact public author identifier, author-local sequence and exact family name. An EdgeId consists of its parent ActId and Binary, A or T role. Authoritative position, finalization epoch and removal facts are not identifier fields. Equal endpoints do not collapse distinct edge identities.

**Definition (References)** · `def:acts:references` PublicReference is an act, edge or exact namespace/name reference. It has no removal state. This slice checks required references against the caller's already resolved set and the batch's declared identities; it neither resolves a repository nor selects an effective declaration.

**Definition (Projection ownership)** · `def:acts:projection` A Binary layout owns one Binary projection; a Paired layout owns both A and T projections. Every projection names the same parent and a unique required role. Mandatory projections remain live; removable projections retain their identity and endpoints when tombstoned. Protocol references remain independently required. Neither a projection nor a co-leg becomes an independently validated accounting record.

**Definition (Structural body)** · `def:acts:body` The first local body representation declares its projection layout and named exact integer quantities with explicit units and vintages. Validation preserves these fields without conversion and refuses empty or duplicate quantity names and empty units. This bounded integer carrier is not the later family census, rational valuation or external byte profile; those contracts must supply their own types before use. No codec or canonical encoding is assigned here under (`[ROOT-amend:design:bite-one-internal-envelopes]`).

**Definition (Act carrier)** · `def:acts:carrier` AcceptedAct is the complete candidate: identifier, author, family, structural body, mandatory and removable projection sets, immutable protocol references, public authentication evidence, finalization epoch and authoritative position. The author and family must agree with the identity. Nonempty authentication evidence is retained as public content; its authenticity is not inferred from that local check.

**Definition (Local validation)** · `def:acts:validation` validate_record validates the complete batch and returns a borrowed ValidatedRecords view. Duplicate act or edge identities, missing required references, missing co-legs and inconsistent local fields return distinct ValidationError variants. The view returns whole acts without cloning, flattening, sorting by host position or mutating input. Borrowing keeps the validated snapshot immutable. Every public operation is labelled and accounted at every observation level; payloads are captured only at trace. The executable owns bootstrap. There are no optional features and no production codec or graph dependency.

**Amendment (First slice evidence)** · `amend:acts:first-slice-evidence` The supported premises for (`[ROOT-gate:design:bite-1]`) are: The finite first-slice structural fixtures and the records entry runtime comparison; no closure partition, effective declaration, public-reference resolver, boundary assembler, shared suite or property tier is claimed. Their test-site evidence is (`claim:acts:identity-is-structural`), (`claim:acts:complete-acts-are-counted-once`), (`claim:acts:duplicates-refuse-and-parallel-identities-survive`), (`claim:acts:both-co-legs-are-required`), (`claim:acts:protocol-references-outlive-dependency-removal`), (`claim:acts:invalid-local-fields-refuse`), (`[ROOT-claim:discipline:records-entry-is-observed-without-changing-results]`). The gate remains held for the rest of bite 1; the caller supplies resolved references and no partition algorithm or family formation verdict is inferred.
